From: CoreNode homelab <noreply@corenode.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm53: fit TileLang NoPE DSA in SM120 shared memory

Consumer Blackwell exposes 101,376 bytes of dynamic shared memory per block.
TileLang's generic 64/2/256 launch requests 169,984 bytes for GLM-5.3's
512-dimensional no-RoPE sparse attention and fails before the first forward.
Use the existing 32-entry, one-stage, 128-thread kernel shape only on
SM120/SM121. Preserve every non-SM12 CUDA and HIP launch unchanged.

---
diff --git a/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py b/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py
index 2c1eff2e2e..46d291708d 100644
--- a/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py
+++ b/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py
@@ -1406,9 +1406,16 @@ def tilelang_sparse_fwd(
             if tail_dim == 0
             else sparse_attention_fwd_kernel_v2
         )
-        kernel = kernel_factory(
-            num_heads, d_v, tail_dim, topk, sm_scale=sm_scale, return_lse=return_lse
-        )
+        kernel_kwargs = {
+            "sm_scale": sm_scale,
+            "return_lse": return_lse,
+        }
+        if torch.cuda.get_device_capability(q.device)[0] == 12:
+            # Consumer Blackwell (SM120/SM121) exposes 101,376 bytes of
+            # dynamic shared memory per block. The default 64/2/256 launch
+            # requests 169,984 bytes for GLM's 512-dimensional NoPE kernel.
+            kernel_kwargs.update(block_I=32, num_stages=1, threads=128)
+        kernel = kernel_factory(num_heads, d_v, tail_dim, topk, **kernel_kwargs)
         # Caller-allocated LSE (in-place kernel arg): written only by kernels
         # traced with return_lse=True, but the prim_func signature always has it.
         lse = torch.empty(
